{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:5ed64733df0533ac","name":"The B'omarr Order","source":{"id":"source:reference-5ed64733df0533ac","title":"The B'omarr Order","revision":20599,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:09:36Z","sha256":"fb5f5f4a273d4d84880002bc1d1a72ab295ee210ced665c982c2ac7329229c1d","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20599","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20B%27omarr%20Order&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-5ed64733df0533ac","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"a","children":["B'omarr Monks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/B%27omarr_Monks"}," are members of a religious order on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"}," that believes that the mind can be expanded to reach a state of enlightenment, which requires a withdrawal from all physical sensation. Once a monk has achieved enlightenment, the Order removes the brain from the enlightened monk's body and places it in a preserving container attached to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["BT-16 Perimeter Security Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/BT-16_Perimeter_Security_Droid","referenceId":"reference:47739f07eea2fe6c"},". Attachment to the BT-16 gives the enlightened monk mobility without the necessity of a mortal body. Enlightened ",{"tag":"a","children":["B'omarr Monks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/B%27omarr_Monks"}," use telepathic commands to interface with their Droids' processors and command the Droids.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["B'omarr Order Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Nonheroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":